/-
# Actual native Jordan product in independent compact Tits matrix formulas

First-party source consuming both checked actual native square components.
The target operation is written from matrix multiplication, real trace and
polynomial adjugate, independently of the native operation and its inverse
coordinate map. Cubic-norm certification is a separate target.

The ordinary formula is the compact real second-Tits convention of
McCrimmon, A Taste of Jordan Algebras (2004), II.4.5.3 pp.196–197 and
C.4.4 p.495, at M3(C), conjugate transpose, u=I, mu=1. The signed gauge is
B=-conj Z. The dedicated literature reviewer read the formula/scope in
native-tits-square-next.md §11; this is not a novelty claim.

Inherited attribution is preserved in NativeTitsVisibleSquare and its
dependencies: compact-albert-recognition commit
40d3b344180d9ddb78aaa2876873377c1e631515, Apache-2.0 with complete notice.
All new adapters and proofs below are locally authored, not copied source.
Thanks to the compact-albert-recognition, Lean and mathlib contributors.
“If I have seen further it is by standing on the sholders of Giants.” — Isaac Newton, letter to Robert Hooke, 1676.
Quotation source: https://www.newtonproject.ox.ac.uk/view/texts/normalized/OTHE00018
