The shift sends `e_j` to `e_(j+1)`, the clock has diagonal `omega^j`, and the
matrix representatives have order `X^b D_b Z^a`. The coordinates `y a b k`
parametrize all off-diagonal anti-Hermitian entries, without a support
restriction on the original variation.

This module transports the actual cyclic pair equations to their Fourier
recurrence. The matrix derivative bridge and the dimension count are separate.
Mathematical source: the architecture manuscript, §6.4, equations (6.6)–(6.7).
All proofs below are original; this file imports mathlib rather than copying its
implementation. Dependency: https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4,
commit 065356127b1dc0016f66b7283ce0ce2c4055aa55, Apache-2.0. The imports above
provide the complex, square-root, finite-index and algebraic tactic APIs;
no upstream declaration was modified. Thanks to the mathlib contributors.
